# Performance and Reliability Guardrails Rule

## Performance
- Define measurable targets (latency, throughput, render time, startup time) per module.
- Avoid unbounded loops/queries and unnecessary heavy computation on critical paths.
- Use efficient data access patterns and pagination where relevant.

## Reliability
- Add timeout/retry/circuit-breaker strategy for unstable dependencies.
- Ensure idempotency for retry-prone write operations when applicable.
- Ensure graceful degradation and clear fallback behavior.

## Operability
- Emit useful logs/metrics/traces for incident triage.
- No major feature closure without runtime verification plan.
- Regressions in critical performance KPIs block gate signoff unless waived.
